 sequences [5]. Motivated by this, one of the main objectives of this paper is to explore the interlacing property of the polynomial sequence {\\{{H}_{n}^{[m]}(1,t)\\}}_{n\\ge 1}${\\{{H}_{n}^{[m]}(1,t)\\}}_{n\\ge 1}$ for any fixed $m\\ge 1$.\n\nFor the purpose of describing our main theorem, we need the following definitions and notations. Given two real-rooted polynomials $f(t)$, $g(t)$ with real coefficients, let $\\{{u}_{i}\\}$ and $\\{{v}_{j}\\}$ be all zeros of $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ in weakly decreasing order, respectively. We say that $g(t)$ interlaces $f(t)$ if $\\mathrm{deg}f(t)=\\mathrm{deg}g(t)+1=n$ and{u}_{n}\\le {v}_{n-1}\\le {u}_{n-1}\\le \\cdots \\le {v}_{2}\\le {u}_{2}\\le {v}_{1}\\le {u}_{1}.${u}_{n}\\le {v}_{n-1}\\le {u}_{n-1}\\le \\cdots \\le {v}_{2}\\le {u}_{2}\\le {v}_{1}\\le {u}_{1}.$ We say that $g(t)$ alternates left of $f(t)$ if $\\mathrm{deg}f(t)=\\mathrm{deg}g(t)=n$ and{v}_{n}\\le {u}_{n}\\le {v}_{n-1}\\le {u}_{n-1}\\le \\cdots \\le {v}_{2}\\le {u}_{2}\\le {v}_{1}\\le {u}_{1}.${v}_{n}\\le {u}_{n}\\le {v}_{n-1}\\le {u}_{n-1}\\le \\cdots \\le {v}_{2}\\le {u}_{2}\\le {v}_{1}\\le {u}_{1}.$ Denote by $g(t)⪯f(t)$ if either $g(t)$ interlaces $f(t)$ or $g(t)$ alternates left of $f(t)$. We say that $g(t)$ strictly interlaces (resp., strictly alternates left of) $f(t)$ if no equality holds in (1.2) (resp., (1.3)). Write $g(t)\\prec f(t)$ if $g(t)$ strictly interlaces or strictly alternates left of $f(t)$. For convenience, we also let $a⪯bx+c$ for any nonnegative real numbers $a,b,c$, and $f(t)⪯0$, $0⪯f(t)$ for any real polynomial $f(t)$ with only real zeros. A sequence of real-rooted polynomials {\\{{f}_{n}(t)\\}}_{n\\ge 0}${\\{{f}_{n}(t)\\}}_{n\\ge 0}$ is said to be a Sturm sequence if${f}_{0}(t)\\prec {f}_{1}(t)\\prec \\cdots \\prec {f}_{n}(t)\\prec \\cdots ,$ and it is said to be a generalized Sturm sequence if${f}_{0}(t)⪯{f}_{1}(t)⪯\\cdots ⪯{f}_{n}(t)⪯\\cdots .$ We can now give our main results as follows.\n\n-----------------------------------------